# The script the default set's fixture harness runs stepped (`fixture-test`;
# docs/dev-practices/headless-mode.md, "How the gate runs a fixture") against
# the config in `config/`, which sets nothing of a child's environment. What
# it prints must be exactly `expected`. It touches no file and starts no
# child.
#
# The default set registers the mise package's directory source, and nothing
# else of a child's environment: `layers` says the one source, named mise,
# at the first of mise's usual places under the home directory `/u`
# (`Mise.candidates`), skipped with none, in the window mode, and none in the
# headless mode. A set that drops mise, from its lakefile's requires or its
# entry modules, says `none` for both.
reload
settle
run layers
scene
